Z||000000||Wannabe||05-16-2000||12:31 AM||||Some friends and I have booked the full track at Shannonville for Sunday July 16th, 2000 and will be having a lapping day. Anyone interested in trying their Fiero and their driving skills (novice or experienced) on a road racing course are welcome. Check out<P> <A HREF="http://members.home.net/abanducci/" TARGET=_blank>http://members.home.net/abanducci/</A> <P>for details. Hopefully it will be debut day for the Blue '87 GT!||||reg||1
Z||000001||DaRkLoRD||05-16-2000||12:40 AM||||Where is Shannonville? Is it close to Toronto?||||reg||5
Z||000002||Wannabe||05-17-2000||12:07 AM||||Shannonville is about 1 1/2 hours east of Toronto. You can get all the details about the track at <A HREF="http://www.shannonville.com" TARGET=_blank>www.shannonville.com</A>   It is not the most spectacular track, but it is an excellent place to learn or develop your driving skills. The track is technical with lots of different types of turns, but there is lots of flat run off so you don't have to worry about destroying your ride.||||reg||1
